[INFO] 09-22 10:46:15 run_experiments.py:98] 3.  **Conditions for Real Numbers**: A complex number `z` is real if and only if `z = \bar{z}` (where `\bar{z}` denotes the complex conjugate of `z`). This implies `Im(z) = 0`.
[INFO] 09-22 10:46:15 run_experiments.py:98] 4.  **Roots of Polynomials**: If `a, b, c` are roots of `x^3 - s1 x^2 + s2 x - s3 = 0`, then their conjugates `\bar{a}, \bar{b}, \bar{c}` are roots of `x^3 - \bar{s1} x^2 + \bar{s2} x - \bar{s3} = 0`. Also, their reciprocals `1/a, 1/b, 1/c` are roots of `s3 x^3 - s2 x^2 + s1 x - 1 = 0`.
