[INFO] 09-22 10:46:15 run_experiments.py:98] 4.  **Analyze permutations**: Based on the problem constraints (`a,b,c` are not real and `|a|,|b|,|c| \neq 1`), determine which permutations for `\bar{z_i} = 1/\sigma(z_i)` are possible. The constraints will force a specific cyclic permutation (e.g., `\bar{a}=1/b, \bar{b}=1/c, \bar{c}=1/a`).
