[INFO] 09-22 10:46:15 run_experiments.py:98] 
[INFO] 09-22 10:46:15 run_experiments.py:98] (ii) For each column $c^{\prime}$, there is $c \in C$ such that $a(r, c) \leqslant a\left(r, c^{\prime}\right)$ for all $r \in R$.
[INFO] 09-22 10:46:15 run_experiments.py:98] 
[INFO] 09-22 10:46:15 run_experiments.py:98] A saddle pair $(R, C)$ is called a minimal pair if for each saddle pair $\left(R^{\prime}, C^{\prime}\right)$ with $R^{\prime} \subseteq R$ and $C^{\prime} \subseteq C$, we have $R^{\prime}=R$ and $C^{\prime}=C$.
