[INFO] 09-22 12:48:25 run_experiments.py:98] 
[INFO] 09-22 12:48:25 run_experiments.py:98] where $\Psi(\mathbf{r})$ is the spatial wavefunction of the electron as a function of position $\mathbf{r}$ and $\mathbf{B}(\mathbf{r})$ is the (boldface denotes vector) magnetic field produced by the proton at position $\mathbf{r}$. Suppose the proton is located at the origin and it acts like a finite-sized magnetic dipole (but much smaller than $a_{0}$ ) with dipole moment
[INFO] 09-22 12:48:25 run_experiments.py:98] 
[INFO] 09-22 12:48:25 run_experiments.py:98] $\mu_{p}=1.41 \times 10^{-26} \mathrm{~J} / \mathrm{T}$. Let the hydrogen atom be in the ground state, meaning $\Psi(\mathbf{r})=\frac{e^{-r / a_{0}}}{\sqrt{\pi a_{0}^{3}}}$, where $a_{0}=5.29 \times 10^{-11} \mathrm{~m}$ is the Bohr radius. Evaluate the magnitude of the integral $|\mathbf{I}|$ (in SI units).
