[INFO] 09-22 15:07:01 run_experiments.py:98] 正在获取解决方案计划...
[INFO] 09-22 15:07:01 run_experiments.py:98] <think>
[INFO] 09-22 15:07:01 run_experiments.py:98] Core Principle Identification:
[INFO] 09-22 15:07:01 run_experiments.py:98] - Equivalent capacitance in series: C_eq = (C1·C2)/(C1 + C2).
[INFO] 09-22 15:07:01 run_experiments.py:98] - Energy stored: U = (1/2)·C_eq·V^2.
[INFO] 09-22 15:07:01 run_experiments.py:98] - Error propagation (maximum/percentage error approach): For y = A·B^n, the fractional error is δy/y ≈ δA/A + |n|·δB/B. For C_eq as a function of C1 and C2, use differential weighting: δC_eq/C_eq ≈ (C2/(C1 + C2))·(δC1/C1) + (C1/(C1 + C2))·(δC2/C2).
[INFO] 09-22 15:07:01 run_experiments.py:98] - Final: δU/U ≈ δC_eq/C_eq + 2·(δV/V). Convert to percent by multiplying by 100.
[INFO] 09-22 15:07:01 run_experiments.py:98] 
[INFO] 09-22 15:07:01 run_experiments.py:98] Pitfall Prediction:
[INFO] 09-22 15:07:01 run_experiments.py:98] - Conceptual: Using the parallel formula instead of series; forgetting that U ∝ V^2 (missing the factor 2 in the voltage contribution).
[INFO] 09-22 15:07:01 run_experiments.py:98] - Calculation: Treating δC_eq/C_eq as simple average or sum of δC1/C1 and δC2/C2 without the proper weights; unnecessary unit conversion (pF to F) for relative errors.
[INFO] 09-22 15:07:01 run_experiments.py:98] - Completeness: Failing to combine the C_eq and V contributions into the final percentage error.
[INFO] 09-22 15:07:01 run_experiments.py:98] 
[INFO] 09-22 15:07:01 run_experiments.py:98] Strategy Formulation:
[INFO] 09-22 15:07:01 run_experiments.py:98] 1. Compute the weighting factors for C1 and C2 in δC_eq/C_eq: w1 = C2/(C1 + C2), w2 = C1/(C1 + C2).
[INFO] 09-22 15:07:01 run_experiments.py:98] 2. Compute fractional uncertainties: ε1 = ΔC1/C1 and ε2 = ΔC2/C2; εV = ΔV/V.
[INFO] 09-22 15:07:01 run_experiments.py:98] 3. Compute fractional uncertainty of equivalent capacitance using linear (maximum) propagation: ε_Ceq = w1·ε1 + w2·ε2.
[INFO] 09-22 15:07:01 run_experiments.py:98] 4. Compute voltage contribution to energy uncertainty: ε_Vpart = 2·εV (since U ∝ V^2).
[INFO] 09-22 15:07:01 run_experiments.py:98] 5. Combine: ε_U = ε_Ceq + ε_Vpart; report percentage error = 100·ε_U. Numerically: C1=2000 pF, ΔC1=10 pF → ε1=0.005; C2=3000 pF, ΔC2=15 pF → ε2=0.005; w1=3000/5000=0.6, w2=2000/5000=0.4 → ε_Ceq=0.6·0.005+0.4·0.005=0.005; εV=0.02/5=0.004 → ε_Vpart=0.008; total ε_U=0.013 → 1.3%.
[INFO] 09-22 15:07:01 run_experiments.py:98] </think>
