[INFO] 09-22 15:07:01 run_experiments.py:98] - Trapezoid midsegment: The segment joining the midpoints of the legs is parallel to the bases and its length is the average of the bases, m = (B + b)/2.
[INFO] 09-22 15:07:01 run_experiments.py:98] - Trapezoid area: Area = height × (sum of parallel sides)/2.
[INFO] 09-22 15:07:01 run_experiments.py:98] - Area ratio with midsegment cut: Cutting a trapezoid by a segment parallel to the bases at mid-leg height creates two trapezoids with areas proportional to (b + m) and (m + B) because both have height h/2 and area equals (h/2) × (average of bases).
[INFO] 09-22 15:07:01 run_experiments.py:98] - Linear cross-section: A segment parallel to the bases at a fraction t of the height from the shorter base has length L(t) = b + (B − b)t.
[INFO] 09-22 15:07:01 run_experiments.py:98] - Equal-area level: The fraction of area above level t is [b t + (B − b)t^2/2] / [b + (B − b)/2]; set this equal to 1/2 to solve for t, then x = L(t).
