[INFO] 09-22 15:07:01 run_experiments.py:98] Strategy Formulation:
[INFO] 09-22 15:07:01 run_experiments.py:98] 1) For item (1), let the tag for i be 0^i 1 (i ≤ k). Define S = ⋃_{i=1}^k { 0^i 1 x : x ∈ Si }. For each i, fix a sparsity polynomial pi(n) with |Si^{=n}| ≤ pi(n). Then for S, |S^{=n}| ≤ Σ_{i=1}^k pi(n − (i+1)) where the shift (i+1) accounts for the tag length; since k is constant and each pi is polynomial, the sum is polynomial, so S is sparse. Define M^S(⟨x,i⟩): form y = 0^i 1 x and query y ∈ S; accept iff yes; this runs in time polynomial in |x| (tag overhead is O(1)).
