[INFO] 09-22 15:07:01 run_experiments.py:98]    - Sparsity: For any length m, either m ≠ t(n) for all n, in which case |SL^{=m}| = 0, or m = t(n) for a unique n, in which case |SL^{=m}| ≤ p(n) ≤ (n+1)^{deg p} ≤ t(n) = m (since r ≥ deg p); hence |SL^{=m}| ≤ m, a polynomial bound, so SL is sparse.
