[INFO] 09-22 15:07:01 run_experiments.py:98] - Optional identification: f(ν) is the complete elliptic integral of the first kind with modulus k = sqrt(1 − ν^2), known to be increasing in k; thus f decreases in ν. However, the direct derivative approach is self-contained.
