[INFO] 09-22 15:07:01 run_experiments.py:98] - Use the compound interest formula A = P(1 + r/m)^(m·t) for nominal annual rate r, compounding m times per year over t years. For annual compounding, m = 1; for quarterly, m = 4.
[INFO] 09-22 15:07:01 run_experiments.py:98] - Compute the amounts owed after 4 years for both compounding schedules, then take the difference: Δ = A_quarterly − A_annual.
[INFO] 09-22 15:07:01 run_experiments.py:98] - Round the final difference to the nearest cent.
[INFO] 09-22 15:07:01 run_experiments.py:98] 
[INFO] 09-22 15:07:01 run_experiments.py:98] Pitfall Prediction:
[INFO] 09-22 15:07:01 run_experiments.py:98] - Misinterpreting the nominal rate: using 12% per quarter instead of 12% per year with quarterly compounding (correct is 3% per quarter).
[INFO] 09-22 15:07:01 run_experiments.py:98] - Wrong number of compounding periods: quarterly over 4 years is 16 periods, not 4.
[INFO] 09-22 15:07:01 run_experiments.py:98] - Using simple interest instead of compound interest, or using continuous compounding by mistake.
[INFO] 09-22 15:07:01 run_experiments.py:98] - Arithmetic mistakes in exponentiation or rounding too early; final rounding should be at the end to two decimals.
[INFO] 09-22 15:07:01 run_experiments.py:98] 
[INFO] 09-22 15:07:01 run_experiments.py:98] Strategy Formulation:
[INFO] 09-22 15:07:01 run_experiments.py:98] 1. Compute the annual-compounding amount: A_annual = 6000·(1 + 0.12)^4 = 6000·1.12^4.
[INFO] 09-22 15:07:01 run_experiments.py:98] 2. Compute the quarterly-compounding amount: A_quarterly = 6000·(1 + 0.12/4)^(4·4) = 6000·1.03^16.
[INFO] 09-22 15:07:01 run_experiments.py:98] 3. Compute the difference: Δ = A_quarterly − A_annual.
[INFO] 09-22 15:07:01 run_experiments.py:98] 4. Round Δ to the nearest cent and report.
[INFO] 09-22 15:07:01 run_experiments.py:98] Computed values:
[INFO] 09-22 15:07:01 run_experiments.py:98] - 1.12^4 = 1.57351936 ⇒ A_annual = 6000·1.57351936 = 9441.11616.
[INFO] 09-22 15:07:01 run_experiments.py:98] - 1.03^16 ≈ 1.6047064383 ⇒ A_quarterly ≈ 6000·1.6047064383 = 9628.23863.
[INFO] 09-22 15:07:01 run_experiments.py:98] - Δ ≈ 9628.23863 − 9441.11616 = 187.12247 ⇒ $187.12 (nearest cent).
