[INFO] 09-22 15:07:01 run_experiments.py:98] - Use Maxwell–Boltzmann kinetic theory for gas molecule speeds. The “mean molecular speed” usually refers to the average speed ⟨v⟩, given by ⟨v⟩ = sqrt(8 k_B T / (π m)), or equivalently using molar quantities: ⟨v⟩ = sqrt(8 R T / (π M)), where:
[INFO] 09-22 15:07:01 run_experiments.py:98]   - T is absolute temperature (K),
[INFO] 09-22 15:07:01 run_experiments.py:98]   - k_B is Boltzmann’s constant,
[INFO] 09-22 15:07:01 run_experiments.py:98]   - m is particle mass (kg),
[INFO] 09-22 15:07:01 run_experiments.py:98]   - R is the ideal gas constant (J·mol⁻¹·K⁻¹),
[INFO] 09-22 15:07:01 run_experiments.py:98]   - M is molar mass (kg·mol⁻¹).
[INFO] 09-22 15:07:01 run_experiments.py:98] - For hydrogen gas H2, use M(H2) ≈ 2.016 g/mol = 2.016×10⁻³ kg/mol.
