[INFO] 09-22 15:07:01 run_experiments.py:98] Core Principle Identification:
[INFO] 09-22 15:07:01 run_experiments.py:98] - Hydrostatic pressure relation: P_abs(z) = P_surface + ρ g Δz for a static, incompressible fluid, where Δz is the vertical depth below the free surface along a connected fluid path.
[INFO] 09-22 15:07:01 run_experiments.py:98] - Gauge pressure definition: P_gauge = P_abs − P_atm.
[INFO] 09-22 15:07:01 run_experiments.py:98] - Pressure continuity in a connected fluid: The pressure at a given point is unique and must be consistent whether computed via any connected free surface; differing free-surface pressures are reconciled by height differences.
[INFO] 09-22 15:07:01 run_experiments.py:98] 
[INFO] 09-22 15:07:01 run_experiments.py:98] Pitfall Prediction:
[INFO] 09-22 15:07:01 run_experiments.py:98] - Conceptual: Assuming both free surfaces are at atmospheric pressure; ignoring that the handle’s trapped gas has sub-atmospheric pressure if the handle level is higher. Confusing which height (h vs H) corresponds to the surface open to atmosphere.
[INFO] 09-22 15:07:01 run_experiments.py:98] - Calculation: Using P = ρ g H as if the handle’s free surface were at atmospheric pressure; forgetting to convert to gauge pressure relative to P_atm.
[INFO] 09-22 15:07:01 run_experiments.py:98] - Completeness: Not confirming inequality consistency (that P = ρ g h implies P < ρ g H).
[INFO] 09-22 15:07:01 run_experiments.py:98] 
[INFO] 09-22 15:07:01 run_experiments.py:98] Strategy Formulation:
[INFO] 09-22 15:07:01 run_experiments.py:98] 1. Identify which free surface is exposed to atmospheric pressure (the main jug’s free surface). Define h as the vertical depth from this atmospheric free surface to the bottom, and H as the (larger) depth from the handle’s free surface to the bottom (H > h).
[INFO] 09-22 15:07:01 run_experiments.py:98] 2. Apply hydrostatics using the atmospheric free surface: P_abs(bottom) = P_atm + ρ g h, hence gauge pressure P = ρ g h.
[INFO] 09-22 15:07:01 run_experiments.py:98] 3. Cross-check using the handle’s free surface: P_abs(bottom) = P_handle_gas + ρ g H, so P_handle_gas = P_atm − ρ g (H − h) < P_atm. Therefore P = ρ g h = ρ g H − (P_atm − P_handle_gas) < ρ g H.
[INFO] 09-22 15:07:01 run_experiments.py:98] 4. Select the choice matching both results: P equals ρ g h (and is less than ρ g H). The unique equality statement is A).
